      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T05:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you talking about WifiConnectivityHelper? We used to have a reset method, which is to write a empty list to firmware. You suggested not to have it as it is the same as setFirmwareRoamingConfiguration() with an empty list as input. So we removed it. Anyway, calling updateFirmwareRoamingConfiguration() after mBssidBlacklist.clear() sends a empty list to firmware to reset it. It does exactly the same as the deleted reset method.  In order to reset the firmware blacklist, we have to write to firmware as of today.",
      "parentUuid": "1b99e508_d76aac7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1224,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1224,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "a5a0ff52197cce591787d27150b6be80578cafd8",
